    "## Before you start modeling: what is the computer comparing?\n",
    "\n",
    "From here on, you will build models of the earth and compare them with your data. Here is what happens every time you run a cell:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **You build a model.** You type in layer thicknesses and resistivities. This is your guess at what the earth under Kafadar looks like. It has sharp layers and true depths (left panel).\n",
    "2. **The computer runs a forward model.** It calculates what you *would have measured* with your exact electrode spacings if the earth looked like your model. \n",
    "3. **It compares the prediction with your real data.** The predicted readings are the red line (right panel). Your actual readings are the black triangles. The misfit give you a quantitative measure of how far apart they are."
